Subject: [PATCH] DeepSeek vision: preserve the TensorFold BF16 SwiGLU boundary

Base: patches 0001 and 0002 in this local experiment, over the imported
Christopher Owen 1107 stack and Local Inference Lab vLLM
19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354.

Rationale: paired GB10 traces showed that the compatibility attention path was
already byte-identical to TensorFold.  The first remaining mismatch was the
vision MLP activation.  TensorFold evaluates SiLU in FP32, rounds that result
to BF16, multiplies the BF16 value by the BF16 up branch in FP32, then rounds
the product to BF16.  Preserve that observable intermediate explicitly and
disable compiler fusion for this small opt-in compatibility module.

Scope: the new activation is selected only when the existing
tensorfold_compat_attention option is enabled.  vLLM's ordinary SiluAndMul and
the default TileLang lane remain unchanged.

Provenance: the generic tower and ordinary activation interface are upstream
vLLM Apache-2.0 code ported from DeepSeek's MIT reference.  The arithmetic
sequence is a local AI-assisted adaptation of behavior recorded from
bertholomus/TensorFold@6062066f65a05a7799c09b9aadde0517ded82105
(Apache-2.0); no TensorFold source or binary is copied.  Claude reviewed the
diagnosis, while the paired tensor hashes are the authoritative evidence.

Validation: 24 focused CPU tests passed on DGX02.  On GB10, both 65x103-patch
Etherscan fixtures matched TensorFold at all 102 recorded stages, including
the activation, final rows and 794-token aligned spans, with zero differing
BF16 values.  End-to-end strict served-output qualification is a separate
gate and is not claimed by this patch.

Local experiment only; not represented as upstream-ready or PR-ready.
